9, 7593, 3147, 12195, 10814, 264, 57930, 2974, 378, 552, 10405, 8934, 271, 65498, 24422, 198, 27775, 383, 279, 2574, 45205, 11, 264, 57930, 2974, 378, 552, 10405, 628, 381, 8613, 539, 3679, 9085, 1680, 430, 5956, 2351, 18303, 318, 349, 18845, 3561, 681, 6988, 5978, 303, 279, 2351, 11, 14938, 1901, 28911, 11, 23439, 11, 16850, 11639, 11, 466, 14399, 13, 271, 55025, 198, 32, 25, 5435, 4748, 17675, 1892, 561, 1965, 5435, 39072, 2144, 13, 198, 33, 25, 7021, 1892, 561, 2400, 1965, 369, 7021, 539, 279, 16713, 2450, 13, 271, 5423, 1132, 279, 2904, 2306, 13, 198, 15666, 25], "raw_logits_by_display_label": {" A": 12.979226112365723, " B": 16.867351531982422}, "raw_logits_by_option_id": {"contains_unsupported": 12.979226112365723, "supported": 16.867351531982422}, "readout_s": 3.6127999919699505e-05, "request_id": "sha256:aa368164f5b1dfd80d18c4d2", "requested_score_position": 509, "response_sha256": "sha256:98bf47b0db19f915c338d419ba52093bb5b29c36049ea5d53bbef4d55827e8c3", "response_text": "Based on the given passages, a ruptured eardrum can be caused by several factors such as middle ear infection (otitis media), foreign objects in the ear, severe head trauma, explosion, loud noise, or surgery.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:c31720ceb0f35645fc813f0d9f6f75c3e69ef610ddecbcbe04f6eaa9d1fb404f", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 510, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-09d602e208b1ba374f1ce750", "source_sha256": "sha256:8255b058fed2a25310452e291183226538a28fc48ff2f25045386b081dc39c12", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:A hole or rupture in the eardrum, a thin membrane that separates the ear canal and the middle ear, is called a perforated eardrum. The medical term for eardrum is tympanic membrane.nfections can cause a hole in the eardrum as a side effect of otitis media. Symptoms of acuteotitis media (middle ear fluid with signs of infection) include a senese of fullness in the ear, some hearing loss, pain, and fever.\\n\\npassage 2:Causes of a ruptured, or perforated, eardrum may include: 1  Middle ear infection (otitis media). 2  A middle ear infection often results in the accumulation of fluids in your middle ear.3  Pressure from these fluids can cause the eardrum to rupture. Foreign objects in your ear. 2  Small objects, such as a cotton swab or hairpin, can puncture or tear the eardrum. 3  Severe head trauma. 4  Severe injury, such as skull fracture, may cause the dislocation or damage to middle and inner ear structures, including your eardrum.\\n\\npassage 3:A perforated eardrum or punctured eardrum is a rupture or perforation (hole) of the eardrum which can occur as a result of otitis media (ear infection), trauma (e.g. by trying to clean the ear with sharp instruments), explosion, loud noise or surgery (accidental creation of a rupture). perforated eardrum or punctured eardrum is a rupture or perforation (hole) of the eardrum which can occur as a result of otitis media (ear infection), trauma (e.g. by trying to clean the ear with sharp instruments), explosion, loud noise or surgery (accidental creation of a rupture).\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"what causes a ruptured eardrum\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0017295899997407105, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 529, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 208, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:e6148357936f5a625e3c84a6", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-09d602e208b1ba374f1ce750", "kv_state_id": "reset-