swer to the question:\n\nThe recipe for turmeric roasted cauliflower rice includes the following ingredients:\n\n* 12 ounces frozen riced cauliflower\n* 1/2 teaspoon ground turmeric\n* 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt\n* 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper\n* 2 T unsweetened shaved coconut flakes\n\nTo prepare the dish, you would first heat a large frying pan over medium heat, then add coconut oil and ground turmeric. You would cook the turmeric for 30-45 seconds, stirring constantly, until it becomes fragrant. Then, you would add the frozen cauliflower rice and cook for 2-3 minutes until it is soft. Finally, you would add salt, pepper, and coconut flakes and toss everything together until it is well mixed.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:9f3c2d8922fe0c8b97b7504e5c3f2487cb8299c0350a0c64266bfbc937dc2b58", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 514, "sentence_count": 1, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-0b9fb3708fe5ef63c6465e84", "source_sha256": "sha256:16fbdb87299743b763018e72a0de79d2c7267c93a1e1b6d0336bd9ab2f90d2e8", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Add the garlic, salt, and coriander, and continue cooking until cauliflower rice is tender and is beginning to brown, about 5 to 8 minutes. Prepare the Turmeric Tahini Sauce: Blend the ingredients for the sauce in a small blender or whisk in a small bowl until very well combined.\\n\\npassage 2:1/2 teaspoon ground turmeric; 12 ounces frozen riced cauliflower; 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt; 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper; 2 T unsweetened shaved coconut flakes; fresh cilantro or parsley, chopped for serving (optional) Instructions. Heat a large frying pan over medium heat. Once hot, add coconut oil and then ground turmeric. Heat turmeric for 30 to 45 seconds, stirring constantly, until fragrant. Add frozen cauliflower rice. Cook for 2 to 3 minutes until soft. Add salt, pepper and coconut flakes. Toss until well mixed.\\n\\npassage 3:This Turmeric Cauliflower Rice with Coconut is loaded with turmeric, black pepper and unsweetened coconut. A naturally vegan, low carb, Whole30 side dish!\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"turmeric roasted cauliflower rice\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0010502739996809396, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:80780cceae3db2cefad224e44ddbeee183e337ad1b37c82660f57c71b3ccfdc7", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 515, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 638, "byte_start": 452, "call_id": "sha256:5248cfaba2f35e2f317e3d99", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-0b9fb3708fe5ef63c6465e84", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-067", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 0.23075294494628903, "marked_response": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe recipe for turmeric roasted cauliflower rice includes the following ingredients:\n\n* 12 ounces frozen riced cauliflower\n* 1/2 teaspoon ground turmeric\n* 1/2 teaspoon kosher salt\n* 1/4 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper\n* 2 T unsweetened shaved coconut flakes\n\nTo prepare the dish, you would first heat a large frying pan over medium heat, then add coconut oil and ground turmeric. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:452:638>>You would cook the turmeric for 30-45 seconds, stirring constantly, until it becomes fragrant. Then, you would add the frozen cauliflower rice and cook for 2-3 minutes until it is soft. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Finally, you would add salt, pepper, and coconut fl