eparate bowl and pour over the roast.\n3. Set crock pot to low and cook for 3 hours.\n4. Turn the roast onto one side and cook for 20 minutes after 3 hours.\n5. Repeat step 4 until the roast has the fat side on the bottom again.\n6. Cook for about 2 more hours, usually 6 hours total.\n7. Check if the roast is done by shredding it with a fork.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:e0f83019499d15050f9f1790fa6431cbb6beae96115724138bfa64caaf433e36", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 684, "sentence_count": 11, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-13b56bdb30dfac0dfbdf609e", "source_sha256": "sha256:75dcfa0126d45b853b9704220ac835e2a786f710e8a093b9c03356133cd29932", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:1 After 3 hours, turn the roast onto one side and cook for 20 minutes. 2  After 20 minutes, turn the roast on the next side and cook 20 minutes, repeat until the roast has the fat side on the bottom again. 3  Cook for about 2 more hours usually 6 hours total. 4  The roast is done when it shreds easily with a fork.\\n\\npassage 2:1 Place roast on top of onions and carrots, fat side down. 2  Combine mustard, sugar, Worcestershire sauce, beef broth and red wine in a separate bowl and pour over roast. 3  Set crock pot to low and cook for 3 hours. 4  After 3 hours, turn the roast onto one side and cook for 20 minutes.\\n\\npassage 3:1 Set crock pot to low and cook for 3 hours. 2  After 3 hours, turn the roast onto one side and cook for 20 minutes. 3  After 20 minutes, turn the roast on the next side and cook 20 minutes, repeat until the roast has the fat side on the bottom again. 4  Cook for about 2 more hours usually 6 hours total.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"bottom round roast how to cook\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0008770990007178625, "tokeniz