dentify your orchid, then start with these basic care guidelines: 1  Light - Give orchids bright light, but no direct sun. 2  Water - Water them thoroughly once or twice a week -- more when it's warmer, less when it's cooler. 3  Fertilizer - Fertilize them when they are growing.  Air movement - Provide gentle air circulation for the plant.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how do you care for orchids\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009473499994783197, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 1, "window_sha256": "sha256:1d4548112ad5ca30a1980994863e19e22028ce099a17bfd9070cc09fab2ab8fd", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 456, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 517, "byte_start": 278, "call_id": "sha256:2c142ecbda91ebfead0cacd7", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-248a7df10603824e8169f9c1", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-192", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 0.04648303985595692, "marked_response": "Sure! Here's a brief answer to the question \"How do you care for orchids?\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo care for orchids, provide them with bright light but no direct sun, water them thoroughly once or twice a week, and make sure the water drains completely out of the pot. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:278:517>>You can also fertilize them when they are growing, and provide gentle air circulation for the plant. Additionally, after the flowers drop, you can cut the flower spike back to a node or remove it entirely to encourage new blooms