ext": "To strengthen muscles around the knee, you can perform exercises such as knee bends, TFL distraction, and thigh contractions. For knee bends, stand a foot away from a wall with your knees hip-width apart and your feet pointing slightly outwards. Slide your back down the wall by slowly bending your knees and let the knees point in the same direction as your toes. For TFL distraction, sit up straight on a chair and slowly straighten and raise your right leg until straight with your foot pointing slightly outwards. Squeeze your right thigh muscles and hold this position for 10 seconds. It's important to note that these exercises may need to be modified or performed under the guidance of a healthcare professional if you have any knee pain or mobility issues.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:bb867b436a58237777a9e5411b1fef52ebe51ebc5cbb4a1b996d39021b37a638", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 433, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-24d7d40952e9a439db71520c", "source_sha256": "sha256:d6a1b98da562b5f0d0043e15146eabb01390fa87d59809ac51c5b2df3418560c", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Knee bends \u2013 3 sets of 10 repetitions (reps). Stand a foot away from a wall with your knees hip-width apart and your feet pointing slightly outwards. Slide your back down the wall by slowly bending your knees. Let the knees point in the same direction as your toes.\\n\\npassage 2:6) TFL Distraction. The TFL (Tensor Fasciae Latae) is a small muscle located at the side of your hip just below the crest of your pelvis. When tight and bound up this nasty little bugger can affect the knee by pulling through the IT band and causing pain on the outside of the knee.\\n\\npassage 3:Thigh contraction \u2013 three sets of 15 seconds with each leg. Sit up straight on a chair. Slowly straighten and raise your right leg until straight with your foot pointing slightly outwards. Squeeze your right thigh muscles and hold this position for 10 seconds.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to strengthen muscles around knee\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009966529996745521, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 452, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 246, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:a8743d89d24e67415687f7ab", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-24d7d40952e9a439db71520c", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-198", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 2.6311283111572266, "marked_response": "<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:0:246>>To strengthen muscles around the knee, you can perform exercises such as knee bends, TFL distraction, and thigh contractions. For knee bends, stand a foot away from a wall with your knees hip-width apart and your feet pointing slightly outwards. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Slide your back down the wall by slowly bending your knees and let the knees point in the same direction as your toes. For TFL distraction, sit up straight on a chair and slowly straighten and raise your right leg until straight with your foot pointing slightly outwards. Squeeze your right thigh muscles and hold this position for 10 seconds. It's important to note that these exercises may need to be modified or performed under the guidance of a healthcare professional if you have any knee pain or mobility issues.", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417