est_id": "sha256:05e25c08d2fd924c63d10303", "requested_score_position": 307, "response_sha256": "sha256:87d0ab45f84db3a30def5c7024ab9b96c3c18c0ba01fc05130efb476ef7b5edd", "response_text": "The passages do not provide specific information on what yearly screenings are recommended for early detection of prostate cancer. However, the American Cancer Society recommends that men should make an informed decision with their health care provider about whether to be screened for prostate cancer.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:10b8c5d3dc68eedeb86b2d41b448de1f13514c4939bd674fe8508eee1a4b9528", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 308, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-2b6d3c929d754942810a94e5", "source_sha256": "sha256:6abafde78797b72b30166d2d9f4b844ff96f45cd2199c30df8d4ad5eb6934315", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Screening means checking your body for cancer before you have symptoms. Getting screening tests regularly may find breast, cervical, and colorectal (colon) cancers early, when treatment is likely to work best. Lung cancer screening is recommended for some people who are at high risk.\\n\\npassage 2:The American Cancer Society (ACS) recommends that men have a chance to make an informed decision with their health care provider about whether to be screened for prostate cancer. The decision should be made after getting information about the uncertainties, risks, and potential benefits of prostate cancer screening.\\n\\npassage 3:Prostate Cancer. Prostate cancer is the most commonly diagnosed cancer, second only to skin cancer, affecting American men today. If you are an African American man or a man with a family history of prostate cancer, the likelihood of a prostate cancer diagnosis increases significantly.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"what yearly screenings are recommended for early detection of prostate cancer\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9c