olden brown, turn the salmon and cook for another 3-5 minutes until cooked through. The skin can be served with the fish or removed easily with a knife or spoon.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:afcf18735ef7b12dc25f4cede11ec7b0492f9dec4e7f0cc1890ee9a363c1f88f", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 698, "sentence_count": 2, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-3074c0800c8f94708034d444", "source_sha256": "sha256:3d53090f780aba979596907b5085a5bbbcf65fe8c49b0d02657aed51c0364d28", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:1 Place the salmon fillet skin side down on the pan. 2  Let it cook, undisturbed, for 2 minutes (if it's a thin fillet) and up to 4 minutes (if it's a thick 2-inch fillet). 3  Don't touch it (the skin might stick and tear); set an alarm instead.4  While it's cooking, liberally sprinkle salt over the top of the fish. Let the oil heat through, about a minute. 2  Place the salmon fillet skin side down on the pan. 3  Let it cook, undisturbed, for 2 minutes (if it's a thin fillet) and up to 4 minutes (if it's a thick 2-inch fillet).\\n\\npassage 2:Bring the salmon to room temperature 10 minutes before cooking. Warm a large nonstick skillet with oil over medium-low heat. Season the fish with salt and pepper. Raise the heat to medium-high. Place the salmon, skin-side up in the pan.Cook until golden brown on 1 side, about 4 minutes. Turn the fish over with a spatula, and cook until it feels firm to the touch and the skin is crisp if desired, about 3 minutes more.The skin can be served or removed easily with a knife or spoon.ring the salmon to room temperature 10 minutes before cooking. Warm a large nonstick skillet with oil over medium-low heat. Season the fish with salt and pepper. Raise the heat to medium-high. Place the salmon, skin-side up in the pan.\\n\\npassage 3:Directions. Heat a large non-stick pan over high with olive oil. Liberally season salmon with salt and pepper. Place skin side down in pan and reduce heat to medium-low. Do not move fillets. Allow to cook about 7 minutes or until well browned and cooked about three quarters of the way through.Turn fillets and cook about 3 minutes more, or until still just barely pink in the center.Serve immediately, with the skin side up.lace skin side down in pan and reduce heat to medium-low. Do not move fillets. Allow to cook about 7 minutes or until well browned and cooked about three quarters of the way through. Turn fillets and cook about 3 minutes more, or until still just barely pink in the center. Serve immediately, with the skin side up.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to cook salmon on skillet with skin\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0010693699996409123, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 1, "window_sha256": "sha256:b4991bede34f10a7c07736edb27c1fdd4d85995bd7cc152bc588a3369d743828", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 697, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 405, "byte_start": 328, "call_id": "sha256:a81479fab6395783f7f06363", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-3074c0800c8f94708034d444", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-284", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 0.5363292694091797, "marked_response": "To cook salmon on skillet with skin, place the salmon fillet skin side down on the pan and let it cook undisturbed for 2-4 minutes depending on its thickness. Season the fish with salt and let the oil heat through. Once the skin is crispy and golden brown, turn the salmon an