dacious, disrespectful, forward, fresh (informal) impertinent, impudent, insolent, insulting, lippy (U.S. & Canad. slang) pert, sassy (U.S. informal) saucy Antonyms civil, complaisant, courteous, decorous, deferential, mannerly, polite, respectful, well-behaved, well-mannered.\\n\\npassage 2:adj. brazen, insolent. 1  assuming. 2  audacious. 3  barefaced. 4  brash. 5  brassy. 6  cheeky. 7  coming on strong. 8  confident. 9  forward. 10  fresh. 11  gritty. 12  gutsy. 13  immodest. 14  impudent. 15  insolent. 16  nervy. 17  pert. 18  presumptuous. 19  rude. 20  sassy. 21  saucy. 22  shameless. 23  smart. 24  smart-alecky. 25  spunky.\\n\\npassage 3:Cheeky is a word used by english people like myself. 1. it is a word used to describe someone who does something or says something sort of disrespectful and sometimes rude, but says it in a cunning way. 2. can also be used in a more serious way i.e if you found out that one of your friends has been talking behind your back, you might say that she is a cheeky bitch.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"define cheeky synonym\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0015821739998500561, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 543, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 287, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:d67085d5dafa2652882d0764", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-31be376bafe9d6c77102cbcf", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-290", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": -1