 weeks when the foliage has matured.\n5. Monitor the plant's growth, which typically reaches heights of 25-30 cm, with each leaf measuring between 25 and 30 cm. The plant bears blue flowers and has a strong pungent fragrance.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:2438d93136dd8649a40d28bffe02e4782cd946f9f69294834a4ccc7dd2043b3e", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 528, "sentence_count": 4, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-45694d11d5d1be0e49c36ad4", "source_sha256": "sha256:b6b622f787d99bb994a64d57df366181cfd80b90e6d2da389aa100f53f48f948", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Plant the cilantro seeds. Sow the seeds about 1\u20444 inch (0.6 cm) deep, spaced 6 to 8 inches (15.2 to 20.3 cm) apart, in rows approximately 1 foot (0.3 m) apart. Cilantro seeds need plenty of moisture to germinate, so make sure to water them frequently. They need about an inch of water per week.\\n\\npassage 2:Prune the plant regularly. Prune your cilantro plant regularly, about every five to seven days. It takes about a week for new foliage to be produced and mature. You will have about three weeks of harvest before the cilantro will flower, which is a sign that the seeds are being produced.\\n\\npassage 3:Here is a general description of these herbal plants: Height: The average height of Culantro plants ranges from 25 cm to 30 cm. Leaves: The leaves grow as rosettes with each leaf growing between 25 and 30 cm. Flowers: These plants bear blue flowers. Aroma: Entire plants have a strong pungent fragrance.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to grow and prune cilantro\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0015073229997142334, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_ind