esh pineapple, 1 lb. of peeled and deveined shrimp, 4 cloves of garlic minced, 1/2 large bell pepper sliced, 2 stalks of bok choy chopped into 1-inch pieces, 4-5 stalks of asparagus chopped into 1-inch pieces, and 4 teaspoons of sesame oil divided. You will also need 1 tablespoon of vegetable oil divided. To prepare the dish, whisk together sauce ingredients and set them aside, then heat the sesame oil and vegetable oil in a large non-stick skillet over medium-high heat. Add the pineapple to the skillet and stir-fry it until it is lightly browned, then remove it to a bowl. Add the shrimp and garlic to the skillet and cook for 1-2 minutes, stirring frequently, before removing them to the bowl with the pineapple. Next, add the remaining oil to the skillet and heat it until it is shimmering, then add the bell pepper, bok choy, asparagus, and sugar snap peas to the skillet and stir-fry them for 1-2 minutes or until they are crisp-tender. Finally, return the shrimp mixture to the skillet, add the cornstarch mixture, and bring the mixture to a boil. Cook and stir for 4-5 minutes or until the sauce is thickened, then sprinkle with coconut and serve with rice. Yield: 4 servings.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:64c543e7e163dc8c36d7dae7387309861cd166eaa4d933fdda4d1de654da2ed3", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 843, "sentence_count": 2, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-4651d6036d7a81745d98755b", "source_sha256": "sha256:63b48e85a0addadfb29abf4bfb3c4c5894888944a538b8c8db137e9fd921185a", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Shrimp and Pineapple Stir-fry. 1  Whisk together sauce ingredients and set aside. 2  Heat 2 teaspoons sesame oil and 1/2 tablespoon vegetable oil in large non-stick skillet on medium-high until shimmering hot. 3  Add pineapple to skillet and stir-fry until lightly browned. Remove pineapple to a bowl. Add shrimp and garlic to skillet. Cook 1-2 minutes, stirring frequently. Remove shrimp and garlic to the bowl with pineapple. Add remaining oil to skillet and heat until shimmering. Add bell pepper, bok choy, asparagus, carrots, and sugar snap peas to skillet.\\n\\npassage 2:Hot cooked rice. Drain pineapple, reserving juice. In a small bowl, mix cornstarch, broth, brown sugar, orange juice, soy sauce and reserved pineapple juice until smooth. In a large skillet, heat oil over medium-high heat. Add peppers and onion; stir-fry 1-2 minutes or just until crisp-tender. Add shrimp; stir-fry 2-3 minutes longer or until shrimp turn pink. Remove from pan. Place pineapple in skillet. Stir cornstarch mixture and add to pan. Bring to a boil; cook and stir 4-5 minutes or until sauce is thickened. Return shrimp mixture to pan; heat through, stirring to combine. Sprinkle with coconut; serve with rice. Yield: 4 servings.\\n\\npassage 3:Shrimp and Pineapple Stir-fry. 1  4 teaspoons sesame oil divided. 2  1 tablespoon vegetable oil divided. 3  1 1/2 cups chopped fresh pineapple. 4  1 lb. peeled and deveined shrimp. 5  4 cloves garlic minced. 6  1/2 large bell pepper sliced. 7  2 stalks bok choy chopped into 1-inch pieces. 8  4-5 stalks asparagus chopped into 1-inch pieces.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"spicy pineapple shrimp stir fry\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0012695370005531004, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:bed800ae244445d7015397afa040a18a8bcabfd96e1cf97c540f9ab0acd98abf", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 844, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 906, "byte_start": 434, "call_id": "sha256:28062493940ca6ff6cf27a1d", "disposition": "complete", "el