 than other traffic systems. This means that users of the current version of the app can receive traffic messages as frequently as every half-mile while driving at 60 mph. Therefore, the current version of AT&T Navigator provides real-time traffic updates that are significantly more frequent than those offered by other traffic systems.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:abc6b050117c3d6b12607d7cc9678376bfcb4a559c7ed7303ca7f9260ae1f3ae", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 441, "sentence_count": 1, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-62567cdada71f909bdbee491", "source_sha256": "sha256:261086314029f0e8ba16f80de2a7b3d5dd2798da1a4dd6dea8a593c3dd1b2801", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:HD Digital Traffic\u00b2 is our best traffic solution. HD Digital Traffic receives updates up to every 30 seconds, making it up to 10 times faster than other traffic systems. That means, driving 60 mph, your d\u0113zl 770LMTHD can receive traffic messages up to every half-mile. On the road, a few seconds\u2019 notice can save minutes or even hours of delay. HD Digital Traffic can tell you how many minutes of delay to expect and if there are any possible detours.\\n\\npassage 2:As you drive on your route, AT&T Navigator periodically checks your route for traffic alerts. If there is a slowdown or other traffic alert, it will notify you and give you the option to avoid that portion of the route.\\n\\npassage 3:How do I cancel my subscription to AT&T Navigator? To cancel the subscription and fee you must go online at att.com/directbill or call AT&T at 1-800-331-0500. Deleting AT&T Navigator from your device does not stop the monthly charge.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how much i navigator hd traffic\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009840899992923369, "token