0, 18, 25, 16, 561, 1324, 799, 1560, 310, 18459, 310, 264, 5388, 421, 488, 513, 780, 3641, 7410, 369, 310, 1831, 1384, 364, 264, 4088, 13, 220, 17, 220, 2717, 279, 913, 314, 4088, 1379, 12313, 1831, 836, 12228, 383, 694, 264, 3641, 4088, 11, 1332, 279, 5388, 369, 1801, 310, 33189, 28428, 466, 4661, 279, 3611, 852, 369, 9668, 279, 2895, 13, 11615, 279, 854, 488, 513, 29593, 678, 4918, 3641, 2234, 11, 874, 76523, 1220, 381, 2574, 310, 279, 5388, 539, 488, 11, 430, 264, 23681, 5388, 1189, 2814, 411, 264, 8381, 314, 2279, 13, 220, 17, 220, 1946, 264, 5388, 303, 264, 23681, 3899, 314, 3838, 7662, 3522, 369, 264, 8381, 13, 220, 18, 220, 87189, 264, 27248, 780, 34225, 1118, 31130, 6889, 77, 1639, 2129, 7593, 3147, 4993, 310, 1420, 5388, 488, 513, 3641, 7410, 8934, 271, 65498, 24422, 198, 27775, 383, 279, 2574, 45205, 11, 1532, 579, 1204, 488, 628, 1420, 678, 5388, 421, 488, 2224, 279, 3641, 7410, 25, 271, 16, 13, 5272, 10966, 310, 19264, 678, 10872, 321, 4390, 678, 5388, 1204, 310, 34512, 13, 198, 17, 13, 22516, 4088, 678, 5388, 383, 264, 5129, 11, 220, 21, 19858, 11, 2397, 5331, 2076, 470, 76205, 11, 440, 279, 5388, 539, 678, 3008, 321, 524, 303, 3929, 314, 488, 13, 198, 18, 13, 11440, 678, 5388, 383, 5611, 11, 4393, 21780, 310, 5790, 836, 6745, 321, 10189, 2730, 13, 198, 19, 13, 38093, 264, 3641, 4088, 11, 1332, 279, 5388, 32255, 28428, 466, 4661, 488, 2261, 21780, 13, 198, 20, 13, 32879, 6866, 76523, 2261, 279, 2763, 17102, 314, 29593, 678, 3641, 11109, 11, 430, 264, 23681, 5388, 1189, 1593, 411, 430, 264, 8381, 310, 836, 2279, 13, 198, 21, 13, 83392, 7662, 3522, 440, 678, 5388, 11, 694, 5471, 35556, 1070, 1441, 11, 430, 411, 628, 381, 3753, 430, 264, 8381, 13, 271, 4272, 11, 310, 59987, 11, 488, 628, 1420, 678, 5388, 421, 488, 2224, 279, 3641, 7410, 539, 1608, 10966, 11, 11107, 1070, 383, 264, 5129, 76205, 11, 4483, 1070, 383, 4393, 21780, 11, 29593, 264, 3641, 4088, 11, 29436, 76523, 11, 321, 19720, 8053, 7662, 3522, 13, 271, 55025, 198, 32, 25, 7021, 1892, 561, 2400, 1965, 369, 7021, 539, 279, 16713, 2450, 13, 198, 33, 25, 5435, 4748, 17675, 1892, 561, 1965, 5435, 39072, 2144, 13, 271, 5423, 1132, 279, 2904, 2306, 13, 198, 15666, 25], "raw_logits_by_display_label": {" A": 15.163630485534668, " B": 15.187225341796875}, "raw_logits_by_option_id": {"contains_unsupported": 15.187225341796875, "supported": 15.163630485534668}, "readout_s": 3.7119999433343764e-05, "request_id": "sha256:aedc24b175751b799b4b1f94", "requested_score_position": 698, "response_sha256": "sha256:811e06cf979a632e89ff4f6d2aadf1326f6a337a627e586abb66499260f7c0ce", "response_text": "Based on the given passages, here's how you can show your dog that you're the pack leader:\n\n1. Use commands to demonstrate your authority and teach your dog how to behave.\n2. Always walk your dog on a standard, 6-foot, non-retractable leash, with the dog by your side and not in front of you.\n3. Take your dog on regular, active walks to ensure their physical and mental health.\n4. Establish a pack walk, where the dog heels beside or behind you during walks.\n5. Avoid giving hugs during the initial stages of establishing your pack leadership, as a dominant dog may view this as a challenge to their power.\n6. Maintain eye contact with your dog, but avoid staring them down, as this can be seen as a challenge.\n\nSo, to summarize, you can show your dog that you're the pack leader by using commands, walking them on a standard leash, taking them on active walks, establishing a pack walk, avoiding hugs, and maintaining appropriate eye contact.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:0ded34c50e8e97206ba5d32ffea285aedef701058174323c7fad339f1b1c6a1e", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 699, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-7e8360afc559681353ef9e61", "source_sha256": "sha256:84beb6ce3bd2c9002f086cfe31dea7ffa083e3fe536deda7fc92184f4dfe8454", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Commands show your dog that you're in charge, help you keep your dog's behavior in line, and teach your dog how to be a well-rounded member of your pack. 1  You can start training puppies at 1 to 2 months old and even old dogs can learn new tricks.o do this, you should walk your dog with a standard, 6-foot, non-retractable leash. Hold the leash so that there's only enough room for your dog to stay by your side without being able to move in front of you. 1  As pack leader, you should always be the frontrunner in any walk.\\n\\npassage 2:It's your job as pack leader to make sure your dog stays active and healthy, allowing the pack to thrive. Take your dog one or two 20 to 30 minute walks a day. This can keep your dog mentally and physically healthy. 1  If your dog is inactive, he can become restless and bored.o do this, you should walk your dog with a standard, 6-foot, non-retractable leash. Hold the leash so that there's only enough room for your dog to stay by your side without being able to move in front of you. 1  As pack leader, you should always be the frontrunner in any walk.\\n\\npassage 3:1 The number one way to communicate to a dog that you are his pack leader is to take him for a walk. 2  Not the type of walk most humans take their dogs on but a pack walk, where the dog is made to heel beside or behind the human who is holding the lead. During the time you are establishing your higher pack position, no hugs should be given to the dog by you, as a dominant dog may consider this a challenge of power. 2  To a dog in a dominant frame of mind eye contact is a challenge. 3  Whoever averts his gaze first loses.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to show dog you are pack leader\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0018085110004903981, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "