 dog by your side and not in front of you.\n3. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Take your dog on regular, active walks to ensure their physical and mental health.\n4. Establish a pack walk, where the dog heels beside or behind you during walks.\n5. Avoid giving hugs during the initial stages of establishing your pack leadership, as a dominant dog may view this as a challenge to their power.\n6. Maintain eye contact with your dog, but avoid staring them down, as this can be seen as a challenge.\n\nSo, to summarize, you can show your dog that you're the pack leader by using commands, walking them on a standard leash, taking them on active walks, establishing a pack walk, avoiding hugs, and maintaining appropriate eye contact.", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normalization": "two_option_softmax_float64", "option_order": ["contains_unsupported", "supported"], "order_remapping": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "prefill_s": 0.8625329489996147, "probabilities_by_option_id": {"contains_unsupported": 0.8230011976357517, "supported": 0.17699880236424825}, "prompt_sha256": "sha256:b99ccd9a6aff720aac62a775d1a28d6f0b494fcab831b8d0c2be2dfdf4dc1843", "prompt_token_count": 719, "prompt_token_ids": [1890, 1386, 1761, 364, 279, 4434, 1965, 1608, 1132, 279, 16713, 2450, 13, 271, 41578, 198, 4754, 6184, 1098, 3147, 6184, 416, 220, 16, 25, 29485, 1420, 678, 5388, 421, 488, 2224, 303, 6545, 11, 1438, 488, 2426, 678, 5388, 579, 7465, 303, 1500, 11, 321, 4390, 678, 5388, 1204, 310, 381, 264, 1575, 62050, 4314, 314, 678, 3641, 13, 220, 16, 220, 1394, 628, 1151, 4706, 54730, 506, 220, 16, 310, 220, 17, 3818, 2235, 321, 1442, 2235, 12228, 628, 3827, 491, 27820, 14026, 635, 411, 11, 488, 1220, 4088, 678, 5388, 440, 264, 5129, 11, 220, 21, 19858, 11, 2397, 5331, 2076, 470, 76205, 13, 22041, 279, 76205, 748, 421, 1017, 579, 1132, 3213, 2956, 364, 678, 5388, 310, 4565, 539, 678, 3