enture to kill Lloyd, along with two other men. The jury did not hear about a separate double homicide case that Hernandez is also facing. Hernandez has pleaded not guilty to all charges.<<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>", "option_order": ["supported", "contains_unsupported"], "prompt_sha256": "sha256:9ac583d95bdef7f374566835e7ee681154eeec8023c3cf0d47c757efaaba74a0", "prompt_token_count": 2212, "request_id": "sha256:16c7f0aa82d9a3f40aa7294a", "response_sha256": "sha256:3982b0c747dd545507fa7d31d30505aea23765b728dbc35652ba8c3dd30feac5", "response_text": "Former NFL star Aaron Hernandez has been found guilty of first-degree murder, as well as unlawful possession of a firearm and unlawful possession of ammunition. The case began over 22 months ago, when the body of Odin Lloyd, a semipro football player, was found near a pile of construction waste. Hernandez was arrested days later and charged with the murder. The jury deliberated for 35 hours over the course of seven days before reaching their verdict. Hernandez, who was once one of the NFL's most promising tight ends, signed a $40-million contract extension with the New England Patriots just two years ago. Friends and fans were shocked by his involvement in the murder case. Hernandez had a troubled past, with incidents including fights, a shooting, and drug use. He also faces murder charges in a 2012 double homicide. The case remains open and no one has been charged. Hernandez's family has a strong sports background, and his father was a major influence on him. However, his father died when Hernandez was 16, and his behavior began to change. The case against Hernandez for the murder of Odin Lloyd included evidence such as text messages and surveillance video. Hernandez was accused of being involved in a joint venture to kill Lloyd, along with two other men. The jury did not hear about a separate double homicide case that Hernandez is also facing. Hernandez has pleaded not guilty to all charges.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_