utting: Softwood or hardwood cuttings can be used, depending on the type of lavender and the time of year. Softwood cuttings are taken from the soft, pliable tips of new growth, while hardwood cuttings are thicker and may snap if forced to bend.\n2. Find the perfect branch: Cut the branch from the base of the stem, taking several inches long cuttings with 3-5 leaf nodes on the stem.\n3. Remove lower leaves: Remove the bottom 3-5 sets of leaves from the stem of the cutting, leaving small wounds where the roots will grow.\n\nNote: Passages 2 and 3 provide the most specific instructions for taking lavender cuttings.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:ec6515221589490bf1a885c3b78b944f9aec3af33794c09eae50feb39d01a8c7", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 489, "sentence_count": 3, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-92f4a79f3491e30e3e3bd369", "source_sha256": "sha256:0379e5289b7449f726beae666c439e1282bf043399134ffb707ae5df628a220e", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:You can start lavender from hardwood or softwood cuttings. Softwood cuttings are taken from the soft, pliable tips of new growth. Hardwood is thicker than softwood and resists bending. It may snap if you force it to bend. The best type of cutting to use depends on the type of lavender and the time of year.\\n\\npassage 2:Once you find the perfect branch, cut it from the plant at the base of the stem. Taking cuttings for lavender propagation. Take cuttings that are several inches long. You want the cuttings to have 3-5 leaf nodes on the stems that you can remove, but still have several inches of growth at the top.\\n\\npassage 3:After the cuttings from your lavender plant, remove the bottom 3-5 sets of leaves from the stem of the cutting. You can pinch them off with your fingernail, or clip them off with a sharp pair of clippers. You want to leave small wounds on the stems, that\u2019s where the roots will grow out of.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to lavender cuttings\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009371930000270368, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 1, "window_sha256": "sha256:f55a3782409702c5f82035772c95d9c7eb2b6fed2e7a6c65a48885d7cfe75246", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 488, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 713, "byte_start": 482, "call_id": "sha256:1f05691f623139dd3284082c", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-92f4a79f3491e30e3e3bd369", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-786", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": -1.2417182922363281, "marked_response": "Based on the given passages, here's how to take lavender cuttings:\n\n1. Choose the right type of cutting: Softwood or hardwood cuttings can be used, depending on the type of lavender and the time of year. Softwood cuttings are taken from the soft, pliable tips of new growth, while hardwood cuttings are thicker and may snap if forced to bend.\n2. Find the perfect branch: Cut the branch from the base of the stem, taking several inches long cuttings with 3-5 leaf nodes on the stem.\n<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:482:713>>3. Remove lower leaves: Remove the bottom 3-5 sets of leaves from the stem of the cutting, leaving small wounds where the roots will grow.\n\nNote: Passages 2 and 3 provide the most specific instructions for taking lavender cuttings.<<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normali