"sha256:3f14ea160799f6cd07ca2112", "requested_score_position": 431, "response_sha256": "sha256:57704f5b15913b6edada7eecbf776b818f8cee2b1ce2a4bfc82279a031bb9e2f", "response_text": "A diet to help raise HDL levels would include a daily serving of essential fatty acids from foods like avocados, nuts, olive oil, nut oils, and nut butters. Also, foods high in soluble fiber such as flax seed, apples, oranges, and soybeans can help boost HDL levels. A glass of wine with dinner may also contribute to raising HDL levels. Despite the evidence being weak, olive oil and fish are often cited as foods that can help raise HDL levels and they have other well-documented benefits for heart health.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:700de6b5705787aab8b401be5d64291e9dd7f8cbe069f2eab6374d5de9b234bd", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 432, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-942b84e6be214fe579e7f5a1", "source_sha256": "sha256:8a57eaf799d6df873081eff9d97645a082dafc1bf2c143be140d768a218f80ca", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Good ones are colorful bell peppers, chili peppers, and broccoli. 4. Raise your good cholesterol! We tend to focus on the negative, but it\u2019s equally important to raise your good cholesterol. Do this with a daily serving of essential fatty acids from avocados, nuts, olive oil, nut oils, and nut butters.\\n\\npassage 2:Other Foods that Raise HDL Cholesterol. Foods that are high in soluble fiber, such as flax seed, apples, oranges, and soybeans may help boost your HDL levels. Having a glass of wine with dinner appears to help as well. Olive oil and fish are often cited as foods that help raise HDL levels. However the actual evidence on in this is somewhat weak. But because olive oil and fish oil both have other well-documented benefits, particularly for heart health, I think it\u2019s a great idea to include them in your diet anyway.\\n\\npassage 3:4 foods that boost good cholesterol. These four super-foods increase your levels of high-density lipoprotein (HDL) or good cholesterol, which will help lower your risk for heart disease. Best Health.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"diet to help raise hdl levels\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0015534210006080684, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 451, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 157, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:2609e3ebe96b5b2525a01db0", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-942b84e6be214fe579e7f5a1", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-788", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": -1.7001714706420896, "marked_response": "<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:0:157>>A diet to help raise HDL levels would include a daily serving of essential fatty acids from foods like avocados, nuts, olive oil, nut oils, and nut butters. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Also, foods high in soluble fiber such as flax seed, apples, oranges, and soybeans can help boost HDL levels. A glass of wine with dinner may also contribute to raising HDL levels. Despite the evidence being weak, olive oil and fish are often cited as foods that can help raise HDL levels and they have other well-documented benefits for heart health.", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normalization": "two_option_softmax_float64", "option_order": ["supported", "contains_unsupported"], "order_remapping": {" A": "s