continuously whisking. Stir in 1/4 cup of chopped pecans into the mixture. Finally, pour this sweet butter and pecan mixture over the split sweet potatoes and enjoy.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:a8c0a4f8ad8f14b8bbe67122298eb3126359fe046b4fb8d48127f40c1e5dbd3f", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 420, "sentence_count": 1, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-994dd56cfba6dea8c08fb377", "source_sha256": "sha256:1321ea12c461a3b0eda3efdb129e081cab28213294776668c976aebf3ccb6c18", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Whip the butter with a whisk until it is fluffy. Slowly pour in 1/2 cup of real maple syrup, whipping the whole time you are pouring. When the syrup is completely mixed in with the butter, stir in 1/4 cup of chopped pecans. Split your baked sweet potatoes in half while they are still hot.\\n\\npassage 2:1 Don't preheat the oven. 2  Prick your sweet potatoes each 2-3 time with a fork, then place them directly on the oven rack in the middle of the oven, above the foil. 3  Turn the oven on to 425. 4  Bake for 45 minutes for sweet potatoes/yams that are 2-3 inches in diameter.\\n\\npassage 3:Sweet potatoes are chock full of beta-carotene, antioxidants, and fiber. They are a great source of manganese and vitamins B6, C, and E. One cup of cubed sweet potatoes is 114 calories, 4 grams of fiber, 2 grams of protein, 27g of carbs, and 6g sugar.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to eat a sweet baked potato\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.000826894999590877, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:541a2441f9eaec1e335e7f57ec7c7deb1a2f8eee03f8920e1bb7797218cb0f2d", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-