r to the ground and check that the tire is properly inflated.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to change a trailer tire can be found in the given passages.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:d3bad92251b723887c43279590c91c1d3709581eb3e2eb7c210f94f297ef7f3c", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 525, "sentence_count": 4, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-a3bd6000f235dbcdb010a05e", "source_sha256": "sha256:a7cddb182f0160188280f5f0f5883fe5385bce8584755c63d115e918bfb8b9ee", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:1 Chock your tires on the side that you won\u2019t be working on, and set the tow vehicle\u2019s parking brake. 2  Use your lug wrench to remove the lug nuts on the flat tire. 3  Remove the flat tire from the hub. 4  Install the spare tire onto the hub.  Lubricate the studs before placing lug nuts back on.\\n\\npassage 2:Live Small | Ride Free. 1  Pull over to a safe place, away from traffic. 2  Gather all the tools you\u2019ll need. 3  Use the lug wrench to break loose (about \u00bd turn) the lug nuts on the wheel to be changed.  Drive your good tire that\u2019s on the same side as the flat tire onto the ramp (may require backing onto the ramp).\\n\\npassage 3:1 Gather all the tools you\u2019ll need. 2  Use the lug wrench to break loose (about \u00bd turn) the lug nuts on the wheel to be changed. 3  Drive your good tire that\u2019s on the same side as the flat tire onto the ramp (may require backing onto the ramp).  Make sure the wheel that needs to be changed can spin freely.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to change a trailer tire\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0014781999998376705, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"