op on the front of the needle. To pick up a stitch dropped on a purl row, turn your work around, and follow the directions for picking up a dropped knit stitch.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how do you purl in knitting\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009033370006363839, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 500, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 244, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:198cc8b00c7b5e6db5d281f3", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-b00caab534200cc3fb8116a6", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-966", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": -0.8338537216186525, "marked_response": "<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:0:244>>Based on the given passages, here's how you can purl in knitting:\n\nTo purl, you will hold the needle with the cast-on stitches in your left hand, wrap the working yarn (ball end) around your left index finger, and hold it in front of the work. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Then, insert the point of the right-hand needle from back to front into the first cast-on stitch on the left-hand needle, opening up a stitch. Place the stitch back onto the left-hand needle with the right side of the loop on the front of the needle.\n\nTo pick up a stitch dropped on a purl row, you will need to turn your work around and follow the directions for picking up a dropped knit stitch.", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {"