16021, 303, 9495, 5330, 678, 1765, 14656, 310, 4786, 678, 4752, 1647, 321, 2407, 5893, 13, 271, 55025, 198, 32, 25, 7021, 1892, 561, 2400, 1965, 369, 7021, 539, 279, 16713, 2450, 13, 198, 33, 25, 5435, 4748, 17675, 1892, 561, 1965, 5435, 39072, 2144, 13, 271, 5423, 1132, 279, 2904, 2306, 13, 198, 15666, 25], "raw_logits_by_display_label": {" A": 12.876622200012207, " B": 16.603870391845703}, "raw_logits_by_option_id": {"contains_unsupported": 16.603870391845703, "supported": 12.876622200012207}, "readout_s": 3.596799979277421e-05, "request_id": "sha256:12759e18f6125c7e4a88d656", "requested_score_position": 494, "response_sha256": "sha256:67fc32d465929c17568460d985ea0e40231e5208bb129e49abc0daf01f6b7065", "response_text": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"Learn how to tailor your own clothes\":\n\nTo learn how to tailor your own clothes, start by gaining experience through practice. The more you sew, the more intuitive the construction process will become. Invest in a good sewing machine and ironing board, and practice altering existing garments to fit your body better. Start with simple adjustments such as taking in or letting out seams, and gradually move on to more complex modifications like reshaping armholes and sleeves. Consider taking online classes or workshops to learn new techniques and improve your skills. Additionally, invest in patterns that are designed for your skill level and the types of garments you want to make. With time and practice, you'll become more comfortable and confident in tailoring your own clothes to fit your unique style and body shape.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:0f97d05ded09b7fe6157b8aa956854863d802274753b4d4350f3d8195827a70d", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 495, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-b7d4cc059361dd8f2fe93ddb", "source_sha256": "sha256:15c549d1e72c4d985275dbf51e24993ee778c43507c65052b18d941c397f93d8", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Then there is good old fashion experience. The more you sew, the more you learn, the more the construction part will become intuitive. Here are the tools I use the most often: 1  Iron/Ironing board-If you are just starting out, the iron/ironing board you currently have is probably fine.\\n\\npassage 2:After adjusting the garment's seams, use the pattern to cut the armhole to its old shape, as necessary. Then restitch the side seams and replace the sleeves. On the next page, we'll give step-by-step instructions on how to custom-fit a pair of pants.\\n\\npassage 3:1. First, decide what types of garments/accessories you want to make, and try to gauge how committed you are going to be to learning something new. This will have an effect on how much you budget for your first sewing machine and which type of machine you decide to buy. 2. Get a sewing machine. Choosing the right machine really comes down to budget, personal preferences, and in some cases, the types of things you want to make. Here are the machines I use.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"learn how to tailor your own clothes\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0018548859998190892, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 514, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 302, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:21f4575214cbad9c9bcc5474", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-b7d4cc059361dd8f2fe93ddb", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-986", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "sup