 to install drywall is about $1.50 per square foot. After material and labor are added in, the cost per panel can range from around $40.00 to $60.00. A typical 12x12 room, for example, will use 12 panels.he cost to install drywall is about $1.50 per square foot. After material and labor are added in, the cost per panel can range from around $40.00 to $60.00. A typical 12x12 room, for example, will use 12 panels.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"drywall vs ceiling tile cost\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0012863150004704949, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:9ad2625ea1f750bb66a0b62365b954ef7c273645b70fa693dcfc89d6e0415956", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 721, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 543, "byte_start": 236, "call_id": "sha256:fc9d322f44278a40537a7309", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-c0a47dc76ee63e411a5a9785", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1059", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 2.220783233642578, "marked_response": "Based on the provided passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nThe cost of drywall versus ceiling tiles for a basement ceiling can vary depending on several factors, including the size of the room and the specific materials used. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:236:543>>However, according to Passage 2, the cost of ceiling tiles can be approximately $707 for 1000 square feet, while the cost of drywall can range from $40 to $60 per panel, or approximately $480 to $72