5430e02a3322391093e103b69170ff28454c4535bc15f5c2aa18", "response_text": "To add a paid stamp in QuickBooks, follow these steps:\n\n1. Look for your invoice template that you are using and right-click on it. Select \"Edit Template\" to open the Basic Customization screen.\n2. Scroll down to the bottom section of the page called Company & Transaction Information and look for the box labeled \"Print Status Stamp\". Click on it to activate the status stamp.\n3. If you want to remove the paid stamp from an invoice that has already been paid, first modify the template by creating a copy and renaming it \"Void Invoice\". Then un-check the \"Print Status Stamp\" box and save the changes.\n4. For QuickBooks 2011 or earlier versions, the Paid stamp may not reflect the date the customer invoice was paid. In this case, you may want to manually record the payment date in another field or use a third-party application to track payments.", "role": "training", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:1b46fc9d18769690ea1b9d31ad8e502fe86c924ff30ebf8e3bb2b0ea72b24dd4", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 747, "sentence_count": 4, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-e01b39e5b37818d8a65ee5be", "source_sha256": "sha256:692954f03ddb7542218bacf3664862a348d03ed00909209aff13323feae19402", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Look for your invoice template that you are using, highlight it, right click on your mouse and Edit Template. This will open up the Basic Customization screen. Let your eyes scan to the bottom section of that page called Company & Transaction Information, and you will see a box that says beside it \u2013 Print Status Stamp.Clicking on that box will make a check mark which will then activate that Status Stamp to be printed when it has been PAID.If you email an invoice that has been paid, then that PAID stamp will appear in the PDF document that QuickBooks sends. And that\u2019s how you get the PAID stamp to appear on a paid invoice.Note: www.quickbookstrained.com is now mobile friendly.From the web address you can choose Options/Mobile formatted and the site will appear in all its living colour for you to view. Check it out.et your eyes scan to the bottom section of that page called Company & Transaction Information, and you will see a box that says beside it \u2013 Print Status Stamp. Clicking on that box will make a check mark which will then activate that Status Stamp to be printed when it has been PAID.\\n\\npassage 2:Modify a Template. Before you void the invoice you need to create your template. Click the customize manage templates button. Click the Copy button to make a copy of the template, then change the template name to \u201cVoid Invoice\u201d in the Template Name box.Click \u201cOK\u201d to close the window. Un-check the Print Status Stamp box, then click Additional Customization.lick the customize manage templates button. Click the Copy button to make a copy of the template, then change the template name to \u201cVoid Invoice\u201d in the Template Name box. Click \u201cOK\u201d to close the window.\\n\\npassage 3:(No Ratings Yet) Loading... For QuickBooks 2011, Intuit improved the Paid stamp to reflect the date the customer invoice was paid, as shown in the screenshot below. Unfortunately, a Paid stamp is also applied to vendor bills, and that stamp does not reflect the date the bill was paid.or QuickBooks 2011, Intuit improved the Paid stamp to reflect the date the customer invoice was paid, as shown in the screenshot below.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to add a paid stamp in quickbooks\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0013653870000780444, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 1, "window_sha256": "s