 Use the search function on eBay to find similar items that have been sold in the past 15 days. Review the average sell price, high and low price range, and adjust your asking price accordingly based on the condition of your item. (Passage 1)\n2. Start the selling process by clicking on the \"Sell\" button at the top of most eBay pages. You can either create a seller account in advance or when listing your first item. (Passage 3)\n3. Manage your listing by checking the bidding activity from the \"Sell\" section of your My eBay account. (Passage 3)\n4. Write a detailed description of your item, including any defects or flaws, to attract potential buyers. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n5. Set a starting price and choose the auction format or fixed price option based on your preferred sales strategy. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n6. Add high-quality images of your item from multiple angles to showcase its features and condition. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n7. Choose the shipping method and calculate the shipping cost based on the weight and dimensions of your item. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:1191:1737>>(Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n8. Monitor the bidding activity and respond promptly to any questions or messages from potential buyers. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n9. Once the auction ends or the fixed price is reached, package and ship the item to the winner according to your agreed terms. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n10. Follow up with the buyer after the sale to ensure they receive their item and leave positive feedback. (Not directly mentioned in the passages)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.<<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normalization": "two_option_softmax_float64", "option_order": ["supported", "contains_unsupported"], "order_remapping": {" A": "support