", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0012082630000804784, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:1382be7f5756e85064a6e841d51c90133cc233e63d85a78189390d9296840568", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 693, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 576, "byte_start": 293, "call_id": "sha256:a04b51a5aaa91f4013ddab48", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-ecaab06607bf077b65b419e5", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1299", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 0.11805820465087882, "marked_response": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to remove laminate countertops without damaging cabinets:\n\n1. Shut off the water to the sink and unhook the plumbing fixtures.\n2. Remove the sink and the faucet, taking care to cut around the caulking with a utility knife before lifting it out.\n<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:293:576>>3. If the countertop is screwed onto the cabinets, use a cordless screwgun to remove the screws from the underside of the countertop and lift it off in one piece.\n4. If the sink is an undermount sink, remove the screws connecting it to the countertop and pull it out of the opening. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>For a drop-in sink, use a pry bar to gently pry it away from the countertop.\n5. Remove the backsplash by slipping a pry bar between the backsplash and the top of the countertop, after cutting away any caulk connecting it to the wall.\n\nBy following these steps, you can remove the laminate countertops without damaging the cabinets.", "model_