t in the upper right corner of your Facebook page. 2  Select privacy settings.. 3  Under block lists at the bottom center of the page, click edit your lists.. 4  At the top, under block users, add the name or e-mail address of the person you'd like to block.5  Click block.. Click account in the upper right corner of your Facebook page. 2  Select privacy settings.. 3  Under block lists at the bottom center of the page, click edit your lists.. 4  At the top, under block users, add the name or e-mail address of the person you'd like to block. 5  Click block..\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how do you block your friend list on facebook\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.001197245000184921, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 1, "window_sha256": "sha256:888a1e2331acc742d84ead22d6245a91b03795ca3a18ddc5d8cd3bebb586424b", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 807, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 1109, "byte_start": 720, "call_id": "sha256:9a571a4f7867902629c4d523", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-362c2a7dcdcb2d36fbf8e996", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1486", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 0.2241191864013673, "marked_response": "Sure! Here's how you can block your friend list on Facebook based on the given passages:\n\n1. Log in to your Facebook account.\n2. Click on the \"Account\" tab in the top right corner.\n3. Select \"Privacy Settings\" from the drop-down menu.\n4. Scroll down to the \"Connecting on Facebook\" section 