nnifer Wexton, D-10th\nGerry Connolly, D-11th\nMcClellan said in a statement:\n\u201cToday is a solemn day for the House of Representatives, as Kevin McCarthy became the first speaker to be removed from his leadership position through a motion to vacate. Since day one of the 118th Congress, McCarthy has shown an inability to govern, a lack of leadership over his conference, and an unwillingness to focus on the issues that matter to the American people.\nAbout Kevin McCarthy's short tenure\nKevin McCarthy was voted into his position on the 15th ballot. He served as the 55thspeaker of the United States House of Representatives from January to October 2023.\nMcCarthy told lawmakers Tuesday evening he would not run again for speaker. There is no obvious successor to lead the House Republican majority. A top McCarthy ally, Rep. Patrick McHenry, R-N.C., was named speaker pro tempore, to serve in the office \"for the time being\" until a new speaker is chosen.", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.001552120999804174, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:14dc498fdaceeedb2562b5108eccabbc2b0b946f5e734b7d83ff9b81a454040e", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 824, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 318, "byte_start": 165, "call_id": "sha256:f0ccfbef3170e978dc4b2525", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-701b34bea3fd105ff7046c5c", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1611", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": -1.934662