 combination of star, \u2026strip, blaze, snip. Commonly have white hair over the spine somewhere between the withers and dock. Commonly have four legs with some white hair, many times over the knees and hocks. Commonly have two-toned tails.\\n\\npassage 3:A common misconception is that if the white markings cross the center of the back, between the withers and the tail, then it is a tobiano, if not, it\u2019s an overo. This is simply not true. Many minimally marked tobianos do not have white that crosses the back, and many overos (especially splashed white overos) do.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"difference between tobiano and overo\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.001032086999657622, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 2, "window_sha256": "sha256:ff5c628e1def12b807f931452da3cde9ca4483e60be8f478a79dd2939230e0ad", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 771, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "whole_response", "attempted": true, "byte_end": null, "byte_start": null, "call_id": "sha256:c96b5e2c8a1cb9e6e6dd316a", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-9d98df2154da09a45fd30bf6", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1667", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 2.6960649490356445, "marked_response": null, "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normalization": "two_option_softmax_float64", "option_order": ["supported", "contains_unsupported"], "order_remapping": {" A": "supported", " B": "c