fore your leg is at 30\u00b0, then it probably isn't a herniated disc pressing on the nerve. Before 30\u00b0, the nerve root isn't stretched, and it's the nerve root stretching in the straight leg raise test that brings the nerve closer to the herniated disc (if you have one).\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"why does lower back.hurt when i do.leg raises\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0009554239995850367, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:76840843bbde7cc6c5ce7f860f0a1dee5c032d809f29bb8cb496cc255fb26f6e", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 452, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 383, "byte_start": 203, "call_id": "sha256:c9f5b0410677538ca6c1b0ee", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-c597920022b6bbd7955d2e9b", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1744", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 2.6955718994140625, "marked_response": "Based on the given passages, the reason why lower back hurts when doing leg raises is due to the pressure on the discs between the vertebrae caused by the rounding of the lower back during the exercise. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:203:383>>The weight of the leg press and the pressure from the rounded lower back can cause a herniation of the lumbar spine, which can irritate the nerves and cause pain in the lower back.<<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normali