te their clothes into different groups, such as lights and darks, which can be further divided into brighter colors and reds. Separate sheets and towels from clothes and wash them separately. This step is important to ensure that the laundry is washed correctly.\n2. Make a cup of \"soap nut tea\" by soaking four or five bagged soap nuts in a cup of very hot water for three minutes. Pour the soap nuts and liquid into the wash. Remove the soap nuts from the washer at the end of the wash and let them dry. Repeat this process three to five times until the soap nuts are no longer effective. Soap nuts are no longer effective when they become thin, soft, mushy, and very light in color.\n3. Put dirty clothes into a washing machine that is connected to power and water. Add any liquid laundry detergent. Wash the clothes following the manufacturer's instructions. Once finished, remove the clothes from the washing machine and hang them up to dry or put them in the dryer.\n4. When doing laundry, always check the care label on each piece of clothing to make sure it can be washed safely. Avoid using too much detergent or fabric softener as these can damage the clothes.", "role": "calibration_tuning", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:73ad32dbd62f4cab585bf96393af36056cd5af41ac1470f20c1579c35e71fa8b", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 629, "sentence_count": 6, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-c952fc35d705cd4019c02e83", "source_sha256": "sha256:58a394ad936c0bc6be44fefbba245e35cbab1927e39cfd4a25a11ae85cf8eb52", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:Here is my version of Laundry for Dummies in Seven Easy Steps: 1  Teach the kids to separate their clothes into different groups. The most basic groups are lights and darks, while those can be broken down even further into bright colors, reds, etc. 2  Teach them that washing in cold water is right for colors and hot water is needs for whites. Get them to separate sheets and towels from clothes and to was