e4be853a", "response_text": "On November 28, 2001, 25-year-old Stephanie Hartwell disappeared from her home in Columbia, Mississippi, leaving behind her four children and a tight-knit family. Her sudden disappearance remains a mystery despite numerous investigations and a recent social media campaign to revive the case. The last confirmed sighting of Stephanie was with her friend Lawanda, who has denied any involvement in her disappearance. Stephanie's family continues to hold onto hope that one day they will find closure and justice for their loved one. Anyone with information is encouraged to contact the Marion County Sheriff's Department.", "role": "calibration_tuning", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:3568236dd408c6c98ff5fe2808e76b5351b31a9ebddb8c5960d265208e7f26ab", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 771, "sentence_count": 1, "sentence_version": "carnot-utf8-sentence-v1", "source_group_id": "group-dd012f04fae803dd38aee7b3", "source_sha256": "sha256:011186c5cee03b0b386704616a1d1ef81126497060c6c6518c14cb0d63016f14", "source_text": "Twenty-one years ago in Mississippi, a mom of four vanished after a shopping trip lured by a friend\nThe mysterious disappearance of Stephanie Hartwell is a tragic example of the unresolved cases that leave families in a state of continuous despair, hoping for answers. A 25-year-old mother of four from Columbia, Mississippi, Stephanie's sudden disappearance on November 28, 2001, left a void in the lives of her children, family, and community.\nStephanie was at the center of her close-knit family. With her children, her sister Sandoria, and their mother all living in the same apartment complex, there was a constant sense of family around. This makes her abrupt vanishing even more uncharacteristic and alarming.\nAt the time of her disappearance, Stephanie was in the midst of personal turmoil. She was planning to end her relationship with her boyfriend, Katron, due to his abusive behavior. In addition to this, she had recently had a fallout with her friend, Lawanda. While the reasons for this estrangement remained private to Stephanie, what\u2019s certain is that her relationships were strained at this pivotal moment.\nOn that fateful morning, Stephanie's day started like any other. She prepped her children for school and even arranged to babysit her nephew. Yet, a phone call from Lawanda changed everything. The two were seen together by a neighbor, and that was the last confirmed sighting of Stephanie.\nThe chilling discovery of her unlocked apartment, a filled bathtub, and clothes prepared for her nephew painted a haunting picture. Stephanie's absence was palpably out of place. And the denials from both Lawanda and Katron deepened the mystery. Their resistance to fully cooperate with the authorities, especially when it came to polygraph tests, raised suspicions.\nNow, over two decades later, Stephanie's children have grown up. They've built their own lives, perhaps become parents themselves, but the void left by their mother's unexplained absence remains. The tattoos on Stephanie's body \u2014 the initials R.J.J.T., the butterfly, \u201cSteph,\u201d and a heart \u2014 are permanent markers of her identity, symbolic reminders of a woman who is missed every day.\nCases like Stephanie's remind us of the fragility of life and the importance of community vigilance. As the years have passed, the chances of resolving this mystery diminish. But hope remains. Perhaps someone, somewhere, holds the key to what happened to Stephanie Hartwell. And for the sake of her family, we hope that one day, they find closure.\nAnyone with information is urged to reach out to the Marion County Sheriff\u2019s Department at (601)-731\u20133782. Every piece of information, no matter how small or seemingly insignificant, can make a difference.", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0017877959999168525, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": 0, "window_sha256": "sha256:b7126b6c477ebaf152e03dacff3c414126891cdd3689649c2295e1d8af347c83", "window_version": "carnot-balanced-contiguous-v1"}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 774, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 416, "byte_start": 163, "call_id": "sha256:b1c4219cef7df20a1d837fb5", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-dd012f04fae803dd38aee7b3", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1823", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 2.0239744186401367, "marked_response": "On November 28, 2001, 25-year-old Stephanie Hartwell disappeared from her home in Columbia, Mississippi, leaving behind her four children and a tight-knit family. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:163:416>>Her sudden disappearance remains a mystery despite numerous investigations and a recent social media campaign to revive the case. The last confirmed sighting of Stephanie was with her friend Lawanda, who has denied any involvement in her disappearance. <<CARNOT_FOCUS_END>>Stephanie's family continues to hold onto hope that one day they will find closure and justice for their loved one. Anyone with information is encouraged to contact the Marion County Sheriff's Department.", "model_sha256": "sha256:7e78da5d7e3ae28d178121f58646953305f3e5bd3cb46f4a75584e8b6c6fe169", "native_option_token_ids": {" A": 357, " B": 417}, "normalization": "two_option_softmax_float64", "option_order": ["contains_unsupported", "supported"], "order_remapping": {" A": "contains_unsupported", " B": "supported"}, "prefill_s": 0.9429304639998008, "probabilities_by_option_id": {"contains_unsupported": 0.8832913475242988, "supported": 0.11670865247570104}