 Pour the milk mixture into jars and add more milk to each jar, mixing well.\n4. Cover the jars and place them in the dehydrator set at 110\u00b0F for 5-7 hours.\n5. If using previously made yogurt, make sure it's well mixed with the warm milk before transferring it to jars.\n6. Use yogurt with active cultures, such as Dannon plain yogurt or yogurt made previously.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide detailed instructions on the dehydration process, such as the duration of dehydration or the specific temperature setting for the dehydrator.", "role": "calibration_tuning", "sealed_prompt_sha256": "sha256:b990de4fb028405f7a0ae76fd4e5bd4a8e9b4d6a67960a04edb184fd3a4950f5", "sealed_prompt_token_count": 723, "sentence_count": null, "sentence_version": null, "source_group_id": "group-f72b40d8b0950bb7c05c5698", "source_sha256": "sha256:0d83029af97cfc3c0554e1951e4776fb936f5e65c6ea8c6e65b92fd1e7635993", "source_text": "{\"passages\":\"passage 1:How to make Yogurt in a Dehydrator: Open your container of milk and pour it into a saucepan. I normally make a gallon of yogurt at a time so I use a big pot. Place the pot on the stove and heat over medium heat until the temperature reaches 185-195 degree.f you are using store bought milk I would scald it, if using raw milk, do what you are comfortable with. Milk at the right temperature. Milk at the right temperature. When the milk reaches 110 degrees, whisk in 2 to 3 tablespoons of yogurt with active yogurt cultures.\\n\\npassage 2:The purchased Greek yogurt will act as a starter and produce the cultures needed for the new batch. Pour 1/4 cup of the cooled milk into each jar and stir to incorporate the yogurt into the milk. Add another 1/4 cup of cooled milk to each jar and mix well. Cover the jars and place them in the Excalibur dehydrator.Set the temperature to 110 degrees Fahrenheit and let incubate for approximately five to seven hours.he purchased Greek yogurt will act as a starter and produce the cultures needed for the new batch. Pour 1/4 cup of the cooled milk into each jar and stir to incorporate the yogurt into the milk. Add another 1/4 cup of cooled milk to each jar and mix well. Cover the jars and place them in the Excalibur dehydrator.\\n\\npassage 3:Previously made yogurt. Previously made yogurt. Make sure the yogurt is well mixed with the warm milk. I use yogurt that I\u2019ve made previously or Dannon plain yogurt. Use any yogurt that contains active yogurt cultures not all do. Transfer the milk/yogurt mixture to jars. Place lids on jars.f you are using store bought milk I would scald it, if using raw milk, do what you are comfortable with. Milk at the right temperature. Milk at the right temperature. When the milk reaches 110 degrees, whisk in 2 to 3 tablespoons of yogurt with active yogurt cultures.\\n\\n\",\"question\":\"how to make yogurt in the dehydrator\"}", "source_version": {"corpus": "ragtruth", "license": "MIT", "release_revision": "c103204b9ce28d6bbad859304bf30de72b8ed8fe"}, "state_reset": true, "token_boundary_receipts": {" A": true, " B": true}, "tokenize_s": 0.0016558790002818569, "tokenizer_identity": {"bos_token_id": "248044", "eos_token_id": "248046", "metadata_model": "gpt2", "representation": "embedded_gguf"}, "window_index": null, "window_sha256": null, "window_version": null}, {"actual_last_evaluated_position": 742, "archived_pilot_reuse": false, "arm": "focused_window", "attempted": true, "byte_end": 279, "byte_start": 0, "call_id": "sha256:0dd18fca3c71d4c4c2a4c527", "disposition": "complete", "eligible": true, "error": null, "generated_tokens": 0, "gold_label": null, "group_id": "group-f72b40d8b0950bb7c05c5698", "kv_state_id": "reset-epoch-1890", "label_to_option_id": {" A": "supported", " B": "contains_unsupported"}, "log_odds_contains_unsupported": 1.1333332061767578, "marked_response": "<<CARNOT_FOCUS_START:0:279>>Based on the provided passages, here's how to make yogurt in a dehydrator:\n\n1. Heat milk on the stovet